      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly answers the 'business models' part of the query and provides a clean categorical axis to group companies. Samples are well-grounded: VC firms tagged vc_investment, 280 Group tagged consulting, 23andMe as software_platform is a defensible reading of a personalized-reports product. Values follow soundly from the descriptions."
    },
    {
      "name": "primary_customer_segment",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.78,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly addresses the 'customers' part of the query and gives a genuine grouping axis. Consumer/enterprise assignments are mostly reasonable (23andMe consumer, Addepar enterprise). However VC firms labeled 'enterprise' is a somewhat loose inference since their customers/investees aren't explicitly enterprise; still defensible but not strongly supported by the text."
    },
    {
      "name": "service_delivery_mode",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.5,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A useful new axis distinct from business model. But groundedness is weak in samples: both VC firms are labeled 'api_based', which the descriptions do not support at all and is essentially invented. 280 Group's training/consulting labeled 'cloud_saas' is also unwarranted. Delivery mode is often not stated in these short descriptions, yet confident specifics were produced."
    },
    {
      "name": "industry_focus",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.82,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Strong analytical leverage for comparing sectors across companies. Mostly well-grounded: 5AM/life science to healthcare_biotech, Addepar to enterprise_data. 23andMe as 'consumer_marketplace' is a slightly off fit (it's more health/genomics), and 280 Group as education_training is reasonable given training/certification mention."
    },
    {
      "name": "value_proposition_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Adds a distinct modeling axis on why customers buy. Addepar to analytics_insight and 23andMe to user_experience are sound readings. VC firms mapped to revenue_growth (returns to investors) is defensible. 280 Group to efficiency_automation is a weaker inference from a proven-process claim but not contradictory."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
  "source_groundedness": 0.76,
  "rationale": "The added columns collectively give strong, non-redundant analytical leverage for a query about business models and customers: business model, customer segment, industry, value proposition, and delivery mode each offer a distinct grouping/comparison axis. Groundedness is generally good but dragged down by service_delivery_mode, which fabricates confident specifics (e.g., 'api_based' for venture capital firms) where the source text is silent. Other columns are mostly sound readings of the descriptions, with only minor loose inferences."
